Track 3: The Sargasso Meridian
- Story & Context: The myth of the Sargasso Meridian claims that all lost data packets drift to this silent center of the world, where they knit themselves into a living, musical landscape. Scholars now say that if you lower a hydrophone into that specific spot, you can hear the ghost of a band playing a song that has no beginning and no end. The sailors who heard it simply call it "the hum that keeps the continents from drifting apart," leaving their ships behind to stay and listen for eternity.
